      date: "2010",
      phase: "revival",
      headline: "The blue river",
      narrative: "Denim moved to low-cost hubs, and the vats moved with it. In 2010 Xintang in Guangdong made about 200 million pairs of jeans a year; Greenpeace found heavy metals in 17 of 21 water and sediment samples from Xintang and Gurao, one with cadmium at 128 times China's limit. Similar reports followed from Tehuacán, Lesotho and Dhaka. Most indigo is now made in China; its birthplace at Ludwigshafen closed in 2023.",
